Backend done. Now here's the complete updated API doc for your mobile app:

  ---
  Complete Status Flow (Option B — Strict Re-review)

  [Draft]
    └─ POST /listings/{id}/submit ──────────→ [Pending]

  [Pending]
    ├─ Admin approves ───────────────────────→ [Active]
    └─ Admin rejects (with reason) ──────────→ [Rejected]

  [Rejected]
    └─ POST /listings/{id}/submit (again) ───→ [Pending]  ← rejection_reason cleared

  [Active]
    ├─ Owner edits anything ─────────────────→ [Pending]  ← auto re-review, notification sent
    └─ POST /listings/{id}/mark-rented ──────→ [Rented]

  [Rented]
    └─ (terminal — no further transitions)

  ---
  Owner App — Screen-by-screen behavior

  My Listings screen (GET /owner/listings)

  Show all listings regardless of status. Use status + status_label to render the badge.

  ┌──────────┬─────────────┬────────────────┬──────────────────────────┐
  │  status  │ Badge color │   Badge text   │      Actions shown       │
  ├──────────┼─────────────┼────────────────┼──────────────────────────┤
  │ draft    │ Grey        │ Draft          │ "Continue"               │
  ├──────────┼─────────────┼────────────────┼──────────────────────────┤
  │ pending  │ Yellow      │ Pending Review │ None (locked)            │
  ├──────────┼─────────────┼────────────────┼──────────────────────────┤
  │ active   │ Green       │ Active         │ "Edit", "Mark as Rented" │
  ├──────────┼─────────────┼────────────────┼──────────────────────────┤
  │ rejected │ Red         │ Rejected       │ "Fix & Resubmit"         │
  ├──────────┼─────────────┼────────────────┼──────────────────────────┤
  │ rented   │ Blue        │ Rented         │ None                     │
  └──────────┴─────────────┴────────────────┴──────────────────────────┘

  ---
  Draft listing detail

  GET /listings/{id}   ← use this for preview
  Show a "Continue your listing" banner at the top with step indicators:
  - Step 2: Photos — photos.length > 0 ? ✓ : ✗
  - Step 3: Location — area != null ? ✓ : ✗

  "Continue" button takes owner to first incomplete step.

  ---
  Pending listing detail

  Show a read-only view with:

  ▎ "⏳ Your listing is under review. You'll be notified once it's approved."

  No edit or delete buttons. Lock the form.

  ---
  Active listing detail

  Show full listing with two action buttons:

  Edit Listing → opens edit form
  - PATCH /api/v1/listings/{id} — details/amenities
  - POST /api/v1/listings/{id}/photos — add more photos
  - PATCH /api/v1/listings/{id}/location — update location

  ▎ ⚠️ Important UX: Before the owner saves any edit, show a warning dialog:
  ▎ "Saving changes will temporarily hide your listing until it's re-approved by admin. Continue?"

  After saving → API returns listing with status: "pending" → update UI to show Pending state + toast: "Your listing has been sent for re-approval."

  Mark as Rented → confirmation dialog → POST /api/v1/listings/{id}/mark-rented

  ---
  Rejected listing detail

  Show the rejection reason in a prominent red card:
  Admin note:
  "Your photos are too dark. Please upload brighter, clearer images."
  Show an "Edit & Resubmit" button. Owner fixes the issue (same edit endpoints), then:
  POST /api/v1/listings/{id}/submit
  Response: status: "pending" → show Pending state.

  ---
  Rented listing

  Read-only. Show in a "Past / Rented" section. No actions.
  Active chats on this listing remain open — let owner and renter finish their conversation.

  ---
  Renter App — What changes

  GET /listings          ← only Active listings appear (backend enforces this)
  GET /listings/{id}     ← if listing becomes Rented/Pending, return 404 or show "unavailable"

  Wishlist behavior:
  - Owner edits active listing → it goes Pending → renter's saved listing shows "Under Review" badge, greyed out
  - Owner marks rented → show "Rented Out" badge, greyed out
  - In both cases, disable the "Message Owner" button with: "This flat is not currently available"

  ---
  Notifications the owner receives

  ┌────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │          Trigger           │               Title                │                                Body                                │
  ├────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Admin approves             │ "Your listing was approved! 🎉"    │ "{title} is now live."                                             │
  ├────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Admin rejects              │ "Your listing was rejected."       │ Admin's typed reason                                               │
  ├────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Owner edits active listing │ "Your listing is under re-review." │ "You edited '{title}'. It's temporarily hidden until re-approved." │
  └────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  All notifications: kind = "listing", reference_id = listing_id → tap opens that listing in the app.
